> fw(x: u8) = x where x < 10
> gw(x: u8) = x where x < 5
> equiv fw ~ gw
fw and gw are equal on the domain of fw (exhaustive)
  domain: x in 0..9 by the where clause (10 points enumerated)
> domain gw
domain of gw:
  x: u8, 0..255
  where x < 5
  defined at 5 of 5 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 5 points of the domain
> aw(x: u8 in 0..255) = x
> bw(x: u8 in 0..255) = x where x in {0,1,2,3}
> equiv aw ~ bw
aw and bw are equal on the domain of aw (exhaustive)
> fa(x: u32 in 0..10000000) = x where x < 1000000
> ga(x: u32 in 0..10000000) = x where x < 500000
> equiv fa ~ ga
fa and ga are equal on the domain of fa (exhaustive)
  domain: x in 0..999999 by the where clause (1000000 points enumerated)
> cw(x: u4 in 0..15) = x
> dw(x: u4 in 0..15) = match x { 0 => 0, 1 => 1 }
  note: match has no default arm: other values are outside the domain
> equiv cw ~ dw
cw and dw differ at 14 points, e.g. x=2: 2 vs undefined
